description:
FILED s519a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) as the residue of #3370.

perl-tests/signatures.t:358  `sub t124 ($b = (local $a = $a + 1)) { "$a/$b" }` -- the `local` sits in a signature default.  #3370's pass (Parser2 _lower_local_terms) leaves it alone on purpose: its unit is the STATEMENT, and a refusal at that statement would remove the whole sub definition (every later row of the file that calls it).  So the expression compiler still strips the word and the default reads/writes $a without the localization perl does (scoped to the sub body).

FIX SHAPE: the signature default lowers inside the sub body (p-check-arity / the default binding); the local can open the body's restore there -- `local $a; $b = ($a = $a + 1) if @_ < 1;` at the head of the body is the same thing.  Probe vs perl first (perl 5.40.3: is t124() eq "124/124" with $a restored after the call).

=== s520a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18): DOES NOT REPRODUCE ON MAIN -- left pending for the s519a merge ===
Probed on the s520a tree (main fca3593b + s520a, no s519a code): `sub t124 ($b = (local $a = $a + 1)) { "$a/$b" }` gives `124/124 after=123`, `t124(7)` gives `123/7 after=123`, and `sub t2 ($x = (local $a = 5)) { inner() . "/$x" }` (inner reads $a dynamically) gives `5/5 after=123` -- identical to perl 5.40.3.  The default already lowers as a dynamic rebinding inside the sub body: `(let (($a (if (p-arg-supplied-p @_ 0) $a (p-box-for-local (unbox $b))))) ...)`, and perl-tests/signatures.t has no t124 row in baselines/fail-baseline.tsv.  So the residue is whatever s519a's #3370 pass (`_lower_local_terms`) does to this shape on ITS tree; whoever merges s519a probes scratch/s520a/p6/sig.pl (copy below) on the merged main.  Nothing changed here.
    use feature 'signatures'; no warnings; our $a = 123;
    sub t124 ($b = (local $a = $a + 1)) { "$a/$b" } print t124(), " after=$a\n"; print t124(7), " after=$a\n";
    sub inner { $a } sub t2 ($x = (local $a = 5)) { inner() . "/$x" } print t2(), " after=$a\n";
perl: `124/124 after=123` / `123/7 after=123` / `5/5 after=123`.
